  "term": "Spearman correlation coefficient",
  "definition": "The Spearman correlation coefficient is a statistical measure used to show how similar two orderings or rankings are. In this context, it was used to compare different ways of ordering brain-network vertices and to assess whether the resulting rankings matched closely.",
